# @cover scripts/os/build_root_service_catalog.shs 100%
# @req REQ-005
"""# Root service catalogue native-build contract

## Overview

PID1 can only launch its fixed VFS, net and HTTP catalogue children when the
disk staging tree contains target-native ELF images at their canonical paths.
The dedicated producer builds PID1 and all three children explicitly; bake
remains a consumer and validator rather than silently compiling substitutes.

## Requirements

**Requirements:** doc/02_requirements/feature/simple_os_enhance.md

REQ-005 requires PID1 to launch the fixed dependency chain with concrete,
least-authority child images.

## Plan

**Plan:** doc/03_plan/sys_test/simple_os_enhance.md

## Design

**Design:** doc/05_design/simple_os_enhance.md

## Research

**Research:** doc/01_research/local/simple_os_enhance.md

## Syntax

```text
sh scripts/os/build_root_service_catalog.shs --target <target> --rootfs <tree>
```

## Evidence boundary

This contract verifies the explicit source-to-output mapping and mandatory ELF
validation. The target build and QEMU boot remain separate evidence gates.

## Inputs

The target defaults to `x86_64-unknown-simpleos`.

The rootfs defaults to `build/os/rootfs`.

The caller may override both values explicitly.

Only x86_64 and riscv64 catalogue targets are accepted.

Every target has a fixed expected ELF machine value.

The build script does not infer a host architecture.

It does not accept an unrecognised target spelling.

## Algorithm

The producer selects the target-specific native-build wrapper.

It builds the PID1 manager first.

It builds the VFS service second.

It builds the network service third.

It builds the HTTP service last.

Each build uses its own freestanding Simple entrypoint.

Each output is written below the provided rootfs tree.

PID1 is written to `/system/service_manager.smf`.

VFS is written to `/system/services/vfs.smf`.

Network is written to `/system/services/net.smf`.

HTTP is written to `/system/services/http.smf`.

The `.smf` suffix does not change the producer artifact format.

The producer writes raw target ELFs.

The legacy C disk writer may add its SMF envelope later.

The Simple disk bake stages raw target ELFs directly.

## Validation

After every native build the producer requires a non-empty output.

It verifies the ELF magic bytes.

It verifies the output machine field matches the requested target.

It requires the native-build provenance stamp.

It verifies the stamp's target field.

Any failure stops before the next catalogue image is treated as ready.

No missing child is replaced with a shell or fixture executable.

No host executable passes the target machine check.

The disk bake then independently validates every staged image.

## Failure modes

An unsupported target fails before invoking a compiler.

A missing compiler output fails at the producer boundary.

A malformed ELF fails at the producer boundary.

A wrong-architecture ELF fails at the producer boundary.

A missing build stamp fails at the producer boundary.

A mismatched build-stamp target fails at the producer boundary.

The caller must repair the target build before attempting disk creation.

## Non-goals

The producer does not sign the catalogue images.

Signing requires a release-owned trust anchor and is a separate gate.

The producer does not create a FAT filesystem.

The producer does not launch QEMU.

The producer does not grant service capabilities.

The kernel root-service catalogue remains the sole authority mint path.
"""

use std.spec.{describe, it, expect}

describe "root service catalogue native-build contract":
    it "builds the four fixed freestanding entrypoints":
        val source = file_read("scripts/os/build_root_service_catalog.shs")
        expect(source).to_contain("src/os/services/init/service_manager_main.spl")
        expect(source).to_contain("src/os/services/vfs/vfs_service_main.spl")
        expect(source).to_contain("src/os/services/netstack/net_service_main.spl")
        expect(source).to_contain("src/os/services/web/http_service_main.spl")

    it "publishes exactly the catalogue paths and validates each target ELF":
        val source = file_read("scripts/os/build_root_service_catalog.shs")
        expect(source).to_contain("$ROOTFS/system/service_manager.smf")
        expect(source).to_contain("$ROOTFS/system/services/vfs.smf")
        expect(source).to_contain("$ROOTFS/system/services/net.smf")
        expect(source).to_contain("$ROOTFS/system/services/http.smf")
        expect(source).to_contain("validate_target_elf")
